because it is my rice.

745
01:10:30,931 --> 01:10:34,230
- You are not.
- GENE: I will eat my rice.

746
01:10:34,334 --> 01:10:35,767
We're not gonna eat that rice.

747
01:10:35,869 --> 01:10:37,234
GENE: My rice.

748
01:10:37,337 --> 01:10:39,999
That is not your rice. That is our rice.

749
01:10:40,107 --> 01:10:41,131
- Okay.
- GENE: Oh, I see.

750
01:10:41,241 --> 01:10:42,970
And I tell you what.

751
01:10:43,910 --> 01:10:47,812
I'm not gonna let you out of
your handcuffs tonight, okay?

752
01:10:47,914 --> 01:10:50,542
Because I still have the key.

753
01:10:57,657 --> 01:10:59,989
Oh, I see. I see.

754
01:11:00,093 --> 01:11:02,391
Let me see if I have this right.

755
01:11:03,263 --> 01:11:05,163
You're the warden himself now.

756
01:11:05,265 --> 01:11:08,462
Is that right? Is that right?
Do I have that right?

757
01:11:13,840 --> 01:11:14,864
Okay?

758
01:11:23,650 --> 01:11:25,174
- DUANE: Dieter.
- No.

759
01:11:30,657 --> 01:11:32,022
- Dieter.
- No.

760
01:11:36,496 --> 01:11:37,929
(PASSES WIND)

761
01:11:38,131 --> 01:11:39,689
Oh, God.

762
01:11:40,400 --> 01:11:42,561
Come on, Dieter, open the cuffs.

763
01:11:42,669 --> 01:11:43,761
No.

764
01:11:43,870 --> 01:11:48,364
You, you are on my list right
after Crazy Horse.

765
01:11:48,475 --> 01:11:49,703
Cut that crap, you know?

766
01:11:49,810 --> 01:11:52,438
Because I will do you in two seconds flat.

767
01:11:52,546 --> 01:11:55,606
- Okay.
- Hey, hey, hey. You are on my list.

768
01:11:55,715 --> 01:11:58,149
On my list.

769
01:12:00,086 --> 01:12:01,519
That's right.

770
01:12:02,823 --> 01:12:03,983
(PASSING WIND)

771
01:12:12,532 --> 01:12:13,726
No food.

772
01:12:14,367 --> 01:12:16,597
Go away, there's no food today.

773
01:12:17,170 --> 01:12:18,364
No food.

774
01:12:26,079 --> 01:12:27,307
Dieter.

775
01:12:27,414 --> 01:12:29,780
- You should apologize.
- Okay.

776
01:12:29,883 --> 01:12:31,578
I was just making a point.

777
01:12:31,685 --> 01:12:33,346
DUANE: You should apologize to Gene.

778
01:12:33,453 --> 01:12:37,947
You are not gonna keep me prisoner.
I said you are not gonna keep me prisoner.

779
01:12:38,058 --> 01:12:40,117
Oh, and you are not the one
that I'm afraid of, okay,

780
01:12:40,227 --> 01:12:42,695
because the man who will frighten me
has to be born yet.

781
01:12:42,796 --> 01:12:44,889
- Come on, apologize.
- Okay?

782
01:12:45,031 --> 01:12:45,998
(SIGHS)

783
01:12:47,267 --> 01:12:48,256
Okay.

784
01:12:48,368 --> 01:12:50,666
Gene, I apologize.

785
01:12:52,873 --> 01:12:54,238
Gene.

786
01:12:59,346 --> 01:13:00,438
Gene.

787
01:13:01,481 --> 01:13:04,006
Hey, I'm really sorry.

788
01:13:08,989 --> 01:13:10,047
Okay?

789
01:13:14,594 --> 01:13:15,891
I'm sorry.

790
01:13:16,563 --> 01:13:17,530
Okay.

791
01:13:24,905 --> 01:13:26,702
(SPEAKING FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

792
01:13:36,182 --> 01:13:39,948
(HELICOPTER APPROACHING)

793
01:13:41,321 --> 01:13:44,654
(SHOUTING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

794
01:13:47,827 --> 01:13:49,385
Motherfucker!

795
01:13:57,904 --> 01:13:59,997
(COUGHING)

796
01:14:00,373 --> 01:14:03,240
I think they believe we call in aircraft.

797
01:14:06,813 --> 01:14:09,782
- DUANE: (CRYING) I can't take this.
- Duane. Duane.

798
01:14:10,717 --> 01:14:12,116
- You hang in.
- I can't take it anymore.

799
01:14:12,218 --> 01:14:13,549
You hang in.

800
01:14:14,988 --> 01:14:16,819
I'm your true friend.

801
01:14:17,223 --> 01:14:18,850
I'm your true friend. I would not lie to you.

802
01:14:18,959 --> 01:14:21,120
I will never let you down, okay?

803
01:14:21,227 --> 01:14:22,660
- Okay.
- Never.

804
01:14:25,665 --> 01:14:27,292
- Okay.
- Never.

805
01:14:27,400 --> 01:14:28,560
Okay.

806
01:14:55,395 --> 01:14:56,362
(WHISPERING) Hey.

807
01:14:56,830 --> 01:14:58,161
So, listen.

808
01:14:58,865 --> 01:15:01,390
Once we have got the guards,

809
01:15:02,302 --> 01:15:04,770
we are gonna set up a perimeter.

810
01:15:05,739 --> 01:15:07,764
If reinforcements come along
this jungle path...

811
01:15:07,874 --> 01:15:08,841
(SHUSHING)

812
01:15:08,975 --> 01:15:11,239
They're having some kind of discussion
in the kitchen.

813
01:15:11,344 --> 01:15:14,780
I understand what they are saying.
I just need to hear.

814
01:15:14,881 --> 01:15:17,213
(MUTTERING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

815
01:15:28,294 --> 01:15:30,455
Hey, what's going on?

816
01:15:30,563 --> 01:15:31,757
Silence.

817
01:15:36,169 --> 01:15:37,431
So what are they saying?

818
01:15:37,537 --> 01:15:39,164
What they're discussing is this.

819
01:15:39,272 --> 01:15:42,002
They sent some villagers out
to forage for some rice.

820
01:15:42,108 --> 01:15:44,076
- Yeah?
- They came back with nothing.

821
01:15:44,177 --> 01:15:47,840
Ever since the bombings,
the entire province cannot grow rice.

822
01:15:47,947 --> 01:15:49,608
I didn't think it could get any worse.

823
01:15:49,716 --> 01:15:51,877
No, it's much worse than that.

824
01:15:52,986 --> 01:15:55,955
They plan to march us out
in the jungle and kill us,

825
01:15:56,056 --> 01:15:59,116
and make it look
as if we were trying to escape.

826
01:16:00,427 --> 01:16:04,887
They wanna all go back to their villages
and somehow try to get some food.

827
01:16:05,432 --> 01:16:08,367
The ringleaders are Little Hitler
and Crazy Horse.

828
01:16:08,468 --> 01:16:10,959
- I knew it.
- Okay, so

829
01:16:12,372 --> 01:16:14,431
it has to be tomorrow.

830
01:16:14,808 --> 01:16:16,105
Come here.

831
01:16:17,610 --> 01:16:18,770
Procet.

832
01:16:20,480 --> 01:16:25,577
We are still a day short
of Independence Day, but so what.

833
01:16:26,219 --> 01:16:28,949
Hey, there's no rain.

834
01:16:30,223 --> 01:16:31,713
Tomorrow,

835
01:16:32,659 --> 01:16:34,251
chow time.

836
01:17:37,957 --> 01:17:40,585
DIETER: So then, Duane and I

837
01:17:41,795 --> 01:17:45,322
will go this way outside of the fence.

838
01:17:45,832 --> 01:17:50,360
The four of you will go this
way outside of the fence.

839
01:17:50,470 --> 01:17:54,531
And we must all
arrive at the kitchen

840
01:17:54,641 --> 01:17:58,543
at the same moment
to encircle them.

841
01:17:58,645 --> 01:18:02,445
This is the most important thing, okay?

842
01:18:02,549 --> 01:18:06,883
And then you two,
you will interrogate the guards.

843
01:18:17,897 --> 01:18:21,162
Okay. Where the hell is the tower?

844
01:18:22,001 --> 01:18:23,628
Where's the tower?

845
01:18:25,805 --> 01:18:29,502
Okay. Yes. Those three are in the
kitchen. I think that is it.

846
01:18:29,609 --> 01:18:31,702
I think they're all in the kitchen, I think.

847
01:18:31,811 --> 01:18:34,075
This is it. I'm going.

848
01:18:37,383 --> 01:18:40,113
Dieter, good luck.

849
01:18:55,568 --> 01:18:57,058
Quiet, quiet.

850
01:20:06,606 --> 01:20:12,272
Quickly. Kitchen. Kitchen.
Meet us at the kitchen. Yes? Okay.

851
01:20:35,535 --> 01:20:39,164
Duane, come on.
Come on. Oh, God.

852
01:20:47,146 --> 01:20:50,240
Oh, God, there are six or seven
or something.

853
01:20:56,956 --> 01:20:57,923
(SHOUTS)

854
01:20:58,424 --> 01:21:00,585
Gene! Procet! Come on!

855
01:21:09,902 --> 01:21:12,598
DIETER: Procet! Gene!
Where the hell are you?

856
01:21:12,705 --> 01:21:15,697
Gene! Damn you, where are...
Duane, come on!

857
01:21:15,808 --> 01:21:19,574
Duane, where the hell are you!

858
01:21:19,679 --> 01:21:21,306
Jumbo, don't try anything.

859
01:21:21,414 --> 01:21:23,609
Go on! Go on, run!

860
01:21:23,716 --> 01:21:24,876
Run!

861
01:21:24,984 --> 01:21:26,713
God damn you!

862
01:21:27,286 --> 01:21:28,844
Where are the shoes?

863
01:21:28,955 --> 01:21:33,255
The shoes are always hanging here.
Look for them! Go on, look for them.

864
01:21:34,127 --> 01:21:36,891
This is terrible. This is terrible.

865
01:21:36,996 --> 01:21:38,554
Come on. Get something.
Get this bag.

866
01:21:38,664 --> 01:21:40,529
- There's no shoes.
- Get this bag.

867
01:21:41,067 --> 01:21:43,092
Get as much as you can.

868
01:21:43,403 --> 01:21:45,337
God damn you, Gene!

869
01:21:45,438 --> 01:21:47,133
God damn you!

870
01:21:48,708 --> 01:21:52,303
We have to leave. We have to leave.
The guards will be coming back.

871
01:21:52,412 --> 01:21:53,640
Come on.

872
01:22:26,579 --> 01:22:28,604
Duane. Duane. Not in the open.
Not in the open. Come on. Come on.

873
01:22:49,135 --> 01:22:50,295
Dieter.

874
01:22:52,605 --> 01:22:57,201
Y. C., what the hell happened?
Why didn't you show up at the kitchen?

875
01:22:57,310 --> 01:23:00,108
Gene? Gene, where the hell were you?

876
01:23:00,213 --> 01:23:03,046
Gene, where the hell have you been?

877
01:23:03,149 --> 01:23:05,879
Did you hear the shooting? Did you?

878
01:23:06,686 --> 01:23:08,017
I couldn't get a shot.

879
01:23:08,121 --> 01:23:12,615
Oh, you couldn't get a shot at them.
You weren't there to get a shot at them.

880
01:23:12,992 --> 01:23:15,460
Look at these.
What nice shoes you have.

881
01:23:15,561 --> 01:23:18,257
Where are our shoes?
Where are our shoes?

882
01:23:20,133 --> 01:23:21,293
Phisit.

883
01:23:22,435 --> 01:23:25,097
You're telling me that he took
three pairs of shoes?

884
01:23:25,204 --> 01:23:28,332
He took his, he took Duane's
and he took mine?

885
01:23:28,441 --> 01:23:29,738
- That's right.
- DIETER: Yeah.

886
01:23:29,842 --> 01:23:30,831
- Yeah.
- DIETER: That's right.

887
01:23:30,943 --> 01:23:33,309
So, you were busy getting your machetes

888
01:23:33,412 --> 01:23:36,006
and your nice shoes
while we were being shot at.

889
01:23:36,115 --> 01:23:39,642
Okay. Where was this rifle?
Where did you find this rifle?

890
01:23:40,419 --> 01:23:41,750
Where'd you get that?

891
01:23:41,854 --> 01:23:43,048
Where am I gonna go?

892
01:23:43,156 --> 01:23:45,750
I don't know where you're gonna go.
Where'd you get the rifle?

893
01:23:45,858 --> 01:23:49,487
Or did you just find that?
You just found it lying around?

894
01:23:50,463 --> 01:23:51,555
We found it.

895
01:23:51,664 --> 01:23:53,097
Okay, listen, that's it.

896
01:23:53,199 --> 01:23:56,327
Listen, I have an ammo clip for you.

897
01:23:56,435 --> 01:23:59,029
My ammo clip for your machete.

898
01:23:59,405 --> 01:24:00,633
Oh, yeah.

899
01:24:03,009 --> 01:24:04,601
DIETER: Oh, that's funny?

900
01:24:04,977 --> 01:24:08,105
- Why is that funny?
- 'Cause I was just thinking,

901
01:24:08,548 --> 01:24:13,008
maybe you'll go back
and get one yourself.

902
01:24:13,119 --> 01:24:15,087
Maybe I'll go back
and get one myself? Okay.

903
01:24:15,188 --> 01:24:17,122
GENE: Happy now
you got to do your big plan?

904
01:24:17,223 --> 01:24:18,212
Yes.

905
01:24:18,324 --> 01:24:19,655
Yes.

906
01:24:19,959 --> 01:24:21,927
Yeah, I bet you're happy.

907
01:24:30,102 --> 01:24:31,797
You hand me that machete.

908
01:24:31,904 --> 01:24:33,496
You hand me that machete.

909
01:24:33,606 --> 01:24:35,540
You tell me where to go.

910
01:24:38,244 --> 01:24:40,178
You tell me where to go.

911
01:24:42,548 --> 01:24:44,743
I don't know where you can go.

912
01:24:46,352 --> 01:24:47,979
I didn't think so.

913
01:24:48,521 --> 01:24:50,045
Didn't think so.

914
01:24:54,760 --> 01:24:56,853
Gene. Gene.

915
01:24:56,963 --> 01:24:58,487
What's that? What's that?

916
01:24:58,598 --> 01:25:00,031
Yeah, Dieter.

917
01:25:01,100 --> 01:25:03,261
Is that where you're going?

918
01:25:03,369 --> 01:25:07,703
See you, Duane. Duane, love you, brother.
You go that way, I'll go this way.

919
01:25:10,009 --> 01:25:11,943
But where am I gonna go?

920
01:25:14,680 --> 01:25:16,511
I'm gonna go over there.

921
01:25:17,917 --> 01:25:19,748
Where am I gonna go?

922
01:25:24,190 --> 01:25:25,953
Where am I gonna go?

923
01:25:45,709 --> 01:25:46,869
Dieter.

924
01:25:48,812 --> 01:25:50,370
It's gonna rain.

925
01:25:51,181 --> 01:25:52,273
I know it.

926
01:25:52,382 --> 01:25:54,543
This is how it always starts.

927
01:26:33,957 --> 01:26:35,584
(SCREAMING)

928
01:27:23,473 --> 01:27:24,599
DIETER: Duane.

929
01:27:27,611 --> 01:27:29,044
Look at this.

930
01:27:29,146 --> 01:27:31,637
You see over there?

931
01:27:33,850 --> 01:27:35,147
See?

932
01:27:36,153 --> 01:27:38,212
Down there must be a river.

933
01:27:38,322 --> 01:27:40,517
It must lead to the Big Muddy.

934
01:27:41,258 --> 01:27:43,453
And then we'll be out of here.

935
01:27:44,061 --> 01:27:47,258
DIETER: We'll build a raft, and we
can float all the way down to it.

936
01:27:47,364 --> 01:27:48,763
No one will see us.

937
01:27:48,865 --> 01:27:51,425
Then we can cross
over into Thailand.

938
01:27:53,237 --> 01:27:55,296
(CUTTING)

939
01:29:47,784 --> 01:29:49,251
Listen.

940
01:29:49,986 --> 01:29:51,578
Do you hear that?

941
01:29:54,024 --> 01:29:55,753
Is that a waterfall?

942
01:30:05,635 --> 01:30:08,263
Waterfall! Waterfall, bail out!

943
01:30:09,439 --> 01:30:10,736
Dieter!

944
01:30:12,409 --> 01:30:14,536
(SHOUTING)

945
01:30:22,786 --> 01:30:23,946
Dieter!

946
01:30:35,866 --> 01:30:37,834
- Careful!
- The shore!

947
01:30:38,335 --> 01:30:39,825
Grab the shore!

948
01:33:54,898 --> 01:33:57,833
Hey, pick a hand.

949
01:34:01,171 --> 01:34:02,160
No.

950
01:34:08,411 --> 01:34:10,902
Which one of your feet is worse off?

951
01:34:11,414 --> 01:34:13,678
That's a trick question, right?

952
01:34:21,958 --> 01:34:24,051
We can trade off with this thing.

953
01:34:25,729 --> 01:34:29,290
DIETER: There's no way
that we shoot it out with the Vietcong

954
01:34:29,399 --> 01:34:31,128
if we run into them, so...

955
01:34:32,302 --> 01:34:35,829
And we can't use these for hunting
because of the noise.

956
01:34:38,842 --> 01:34:40,605
You wanna ditch them?

957
01:34:42,245 --> 01:34:43,303
Yeah.

958
01:34:53,356 --> 01:34:55,824
I'm sick of carrying these, anyway.

959
01:35:10,974 --> 01:35:12,271
(GROANING)

960
01:35:21,384 --> 01:35:22,544
Oh, God.

961
01:35:53,583 --> 01:35:54,709
Duane.

962
01:35:57,053 --> 01:35:58,213
We got to move.

963
01:35:58,321 --> 01:35:59,788
I'm too tired.

964
01:35:59,889 --> 01:36:02,357
- Keep moving.
- No, I'm too tired.

965
01:36:03,393 --> 01:36:04,883
Come on, buddy.

966
01:36:07,430 --> 01:36:09,398
I can't go on any longer.

967
01:36:46,936 --> 01:36:48,062
Duane.

968
01:36:49,606 --> 01:36:50,766
Duane.

969
01:36:51,908 --> 01:36:53,535
These are huts.

970
01:36:54,344 --> 01:36:58,007
This is an abandoned village.

971
01:36:59,916 --> 01:37:01,383
This is a hut.

972
01:37:02,919 --> 01:37:03,908
No.

973
01:37:04,320 --> 01:37:06,413
- Yeah.
- It's all jungle.

974
01:37:07,824 --> 01:37:09,155
Be careful.

975
01:37:31,114 --> 01:37:32,581
- I'm done.
- No.

976
01:37:33,883 --> 01:37:35,316
DIETER: Travel by night.

977
01:37:35,418 --> 01:37:37,477
No, I'm telling you,
I can't go any further.

978
01:37:37,587 --> 01:37:39,521
You just leave me here.

979
01:37:40,824 --> 01:37:42,655
We'll travel by night.

980
01:37:42,992 --> 01:37:44,584
I help you along.

981
01:37:44,694 --> 01:37:47,561
When we reach the Big Muddy,
we'll make it across,

982
01:37:47,664 --> 01:37:52,465
and I'm sure we're gonna run right
into an American officers' club.

983
01:37:53,636 --> 01:37:55,194
And we're gonna go
straight into the kitchen,

984
01:37:55,305 --> 01:37:58,297
and we're gonna order a burger
and French fries

985
01:37:58,408 --> 01:38:01,343
and milkshake and ice cream sundaes.

986
01:38:01,711 --> 01:38:04,179
All that sweet stuff that you like.

987
01:38:06,482 --> 01:38:07,915
(HELICOPTERS APPROACHING)

988
01:38:08,017 --> 01:38:11,544
Duane! Duane! There's choppers!

989
01:38:11,654 --> 01:38:13,588
Duane! Duane, look!

990
01:38:13,690 --> 01:38:16,853
There's... Oh, here we are!

991
01:38:16,960 --> 01:38:18,393
Here we are!

992
01:38:18,494 --> 01:38:21,588
Oh, please! Please, be real!

993
01:38:21,698 --> 01:38:25,099
Here we are! It's your buddies!
It's your buddies!

994
01:38:25,201 --> 01:38:26,862
Oh, yes!

995
01:38:26,970 --> 01:38:29,461
Thank you! Thank you!

996
01:38:29,572 --> 01:38:32,302
We're here! We're here!

997
01:38:32,675 --> 01:38:34,006
No!

998
01:38:34,210 --> 01:38:35,768
We're here!

999
01:38:36,646 --> 01:38:38,580
Where are you going?

1000
01:38:39,916 --> 01:38:41,406
We are here!

1001
01:38:42,385 --> 01:38:43,943
Stop!

1002
01:38:45,822 --> 01:38:48,723
You idiots, where are you going?

1003
01:38:56,833 --> 01:38:58,095
Please.

1004
01:38:59,802 --> 01:39:01,030
Please.

1005
01:39:01,504 --> 01:39:03,131
Please come back.

1006
01:39:04,474 --> 01:39:06,066
Please come back.

1007
01:39:28,564 --> 01:39:30,088
- Keep your voice down.
- Duane.

1008
01:39:30,199 --> 01:39:31,359
- Dieter.
- Duane.

1009
01:39:31,467 --> 01:39:33,867
- The guards are coming.
- Duane,

1010
01:39:35,471 --> 01:39:37,063
I'm not speaking.

1011
01:39:38,741 --> 01:39:40,333
I'm not speaking.

1012
01:39:41,778 --> 01:39:45,839
God, why don't you help us
when we need you most?

1013
01:39:45,949 --> 01:39:48,918
Keep your voice down.
They're coming.

1014
01:39:52,288 --> 01:39:54,552
(SHIVERING)

1015
01:40:01,264 --> 01:40:02,561
Come here.

1016
01:40:03,499 --> 01:40:04,727
Lie down.

1017
01:40:13,142 --> 01:40:14,632
Lie down there.

1018
01:40:16,112 --> 01:40:17,340
Lie down.

1019
01:40:18,548 --> 01:40:19,810
Okay.

1020
01:40:22,318 --> 01:40:26,982
Listen, I'm gonna build
a fire tonight, a big one.

1021
01:40:27,156 --> 01:40:29,852
And those helicopters,
they will see it.

1022
01:40:30,159 --> 01:40:31,888
And they will come for us.

1023
01:40:31,995 --> 01:40:34,088
Okay, they will come for us.

1024
01:40:40,269 --> 01:40:42,567
Come on, come on.

1025
01:40:43,906 --> 01:40:45,134
Yes.

1026
01:41:26,149 --> 01:41:27,810
DIETER: (SHOUTING) Here we are!

1027
01:41:28,718 --> 01:41:32,245
Here we are! Oh, yes!

1028
01:41:32,355 --> 01:41:36,018
Oh, thank God! Oh, yes!

1029
01:41:36,125 --> 01:41:37,319
Yeah!

1030
01:41:37,860 --> 01:41:39,259
Yes!

1031
01:41:39,362 --> 01:41:41,592
(MACHINE GUN FIRlNG)

1032
01:41:49,172 --> 01:41:50,867
You idiots!

1033
01:41:50,973 --> 01:41:53,168
You almost killed me!

1034
01:41:54,610 --> 01:41:56,510
(SOBBING)

1035
01:42:50,466 --> 01:42:52,866
I dreamed there was a fire.

1036
01:42:55,404 --> 01:43:00,068
Why did they think a whole damn village
would be burning?

1037
01:43:01,010 --> 01:43:03,205
How could we be Vietcong?

1038
01:43:06,482 --> 01:43:08,575
Now they must've heard us.

1039
01:43:08,684 --> 01:43:10,242
They must've seen this.

1040
01:43:10,353 --> 01:43:14,312
The Vietcong will be on their way.
They could be here any moment.

1041
01:43:18,227 --> 01:43:19,455
Let's leave here.

1042
01:43:49,158 --> 01:43:52,992
(SPEAKING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

1043
01:43:59,101 --> 01:44:01,331
(MAN SHOUTING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

1044
01:44:02,004 --> 01:44:04,063
(DIETER SPEAKING IN
FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

1045
01:44:04,173 --> 01:44:05,697
(SHOUTING)

1046
01:44:37,340 --> 01:44:39,001
(YELLING)

1047
01:45:02,832 --> 01:45:05,130
(SHOUTING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

1048
01:45:37,533 --> 01:45:39,023
DUANE: Dieter.

1049
01:45:42,738 --> 01:45:44,069
Dieter.

1050
01:45:47,777 --> 01:45:49,369
My feet are cold.

1051
01:46:11,801 --> 01:46:14,361
(MAN SPEAKING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

1052
01:47:30,880 --> 01:47:32,108
I'm cold.

1053
01:47:35,017 --> 01:47:36,609
My feet are cold.

1054
01:47:42,825 --> 01:47:44,656
You can have the sole.

1055
01:47:58,641 --> 01:47:59,767
Duane?

1056
01:49:47,416 --> 01:49:49,407
(DIETER SHOUTING)

1057
01:49:51,854 --> 01:49:53,685
Hey, you!

1058
01:49:54,924 --> 01:49:56,551
I'm here!

1059
01:49:58,827 --> 01:50:01,022
Please turn around.

1060
01:50:04,099 --> 01:50:05,623
Hey!

1061
01:50:08,671 --> 01:50:11,333
Don't leave. Hey!

1062
01:50:13,008 --> 01:50:15,499
Hey! Hey!

1063
01:50:19,949 --> 01:50:21,610
Don't go away.

1064
01:50:24,019 --> 01:50:25,646
Don't go away.

1065
01:50:31,093 --> 01:50:32,355
Hey!

1066
01:50:33,295 --> 01:50:35,126
Oh, come on!

1067
01:50:37,700 --> 01:50:39,395
Oh, please!

1068
01:50:39,735 --> 01:50:41,225
Come on!

1069
01:50:49,745 --> 01:50:52,908
Okay. Hey!

1070
01:50:53,482 --> 01:50:57,111
Over here! Over here!

1071
01:50:57,219 --> 01:50:59,619
Help me!
Come on, come on, come on.

1072
01:51:00,222 --> 01:51:02,986
Come on down. Yeah, come on.

1073
01:51:07,563 --> 01:51:08,860
They're coming.

1074
01:51:13,102 --> 01:51:15,127
Yes! Yes, please!

1075
01:51:16,538 --> 01:51:18,062
See me!

1076
01:51:26,849 --> 01:51:27,816
Yes!

1077
01:52:00,449 --> 01:52:02,383
(DIETER LAUGHING)

1078
01:52:27,342 --> 01:52:28,866
MAN: Who are you, buddy?

1079
01:52:28,977 --> 01:52:30,308
Name?

1080
01:52:30,746 --> 01:52:36,150
Flight Lieutenant Dieter Dengler,
U.S.S. Ranger.

1081
01:52:36,251 --> 01:52:37,479
Authenticator?

1082
01:52:37,586 --> 01:52:38,746
- What's your authenticator?
- Rescue Dawn.

1083
01:52:38,854 --> 01:52:40,082
- Rescue Dawn.
- Louder!

1084
01:52:40,189 --> 01:52:41,713
Rescue Dawn!

1085
01:52:41,824 --> 01:52:44,622
- Favorite sport?
- Hunting.

1086
01:52:44,727 --> 01:52:46,922
Favorite fish?

1087
01:52:47,029 --> 01:52:48,121
Trout.

1088
01:52:48,230 --> 01:52:50,164
Confirmed. Confirmed. It's him!

1089
01:52:50,265 --> 01:52:52,426
I can't believe it.

1090
01:52:52,534 --> 01:52:54,627
Jesus, buddy,
you made it out of the bush.

1091
01:52:54,737 --> 01:52:56,170
Bring him home!

1092
01:52:57,539 --> 01:52:59,336
He's coming home with us.

1093
01:52:59,441 --> 01:53:01,932
- Oh, shit!
- Going home.

1094
01:53:02,044 --> 01:53:03,341
All right.

1095
01:53:07,616 --> 01:53:09,345
Way to go, buddy.

1096
01:53:59,168 --> 01:54:00,931
MAN: Easy, easy, easy.

1097
01:54:01,804 --> 01:54:05,399
Hold up here, hold up here.
Hey, everyone listen to me.

1098
01:54:05,941 --> 01:54:07,374
- We're in charge here.
- Back up. Back up.

1099
01:54:07,476 --> 01:54:10,707
This man has been on
a highly classified operation. Hold.

1100
01:54:10,813 --> 01:54:13,748
No one is to see him. No one is
to touch him. No one is to talk to him.

1101
01:54:13,849 --> 01:54:15,942
AGENT 2: Get him inside.
AGENT 1: You'll forget what you've seen.

1102
01:54:16,051 --> 01:54:19,350
AGENT 1: In fact, from now on,
it's a black operation. Is that clear?

1103
01:54:19,454 --> 01:54:20,512
You got me on that?

1104
01:54:20,622 --> 01:54:22,055
AGENT 2: Back up. Back up.
AGENT 1: Stand back.

1105
01:54:22,157 --> 01:54:23,647
All right. Let's go.

1106
01:54:25,961 --> 01:54:28,020
NURSE: You're doing great, Dieter.

1107
01:54:28,363 --> 01:54:30,456
You don't need this anymore.

1108
01:54:34,770 --> 01:54:38,604
(WHISPERING)
Hey, when can I go back to my ship?

1109
01:54:40,742 --> 01:54:42,175
I don't know.

1110
01:55:11,607 --> 01:55:13,700
Okay, go, go, go, go, go.

1111
01:55:16,211 --> 01:55:18,304
You guys are a lot of fun.

1112
01:55:18,413 --> 01:55:22,941
You know, how many times I have to
tell you? I don't know the coordinates.

1113
01:55:23,051 --> 01:55:25,542
Let's go back to the guards.
Tell me about their uniforms.

1114
01:55:25,654 --> 01:55:28,953
There were some with red stars,
maybe they're Vietcong.

1115
01:55:29,057 --> 01:55:31,355
The others were Laotians...

1116
01:55:31,460 --> 01:55:32,722
Oh, no.

1117
01:55:32,828 --> 01:55:34,159
Oh, no.

1118
01:55:36,565 --> 01:55:37,793
Dieter!

1119
01:55:37,900 --> 01:55:39,231
There's my buddies.

1120
01:55:39,334 --> 01:55:42,394
- Happy birthday.
- That's my buddies.

1121
01:55:42,504 --> 01:55:43,664
You made it.

1122
01:55:43,772 --> 01:55:45,865
It's good to see you, Spook.

1123
01:55:47,075 --> 01:55:48,201
Dieter.

1124
01:55:48,310 --> 01:55:50,870
Norman. Oh, my God.

1125
01:55:50,979 --> 01:55:53,174
Gentlemen, can you give us
a couple of minutes alone, please?

1126
01:55:53,282 --> 01:55:54,715
It should be all right.

1127
01:55:54,816 --> 01:55:57,580
I got a little letter from his fiancée.

1128
01:55:57,686 --> 01:55:59,620
It's kind of personal.
You know what I mean?

1129
01:55:59,721 --> 01:56:01,552
Keep it personal, Lieutenant.

1130
01:56:01,657 --> 01:56:04,649
We're in the middle of
a highly classified debriefing.

1131
01:56:04,760 --> 01:56:06,284
Will do. It's from his old lady.

1132
01:56:06,395 --> 01:56:07,953
- Ten minutes.
- Okay.

1133
01:56:08,063 --> 01:56:09,587
Thank you, gentlemen.

1134
01:56:09,698 --> 01:56:10,756
Thank you.

1135
01:56:10,866 --> 01:56:15,599
Hey, Spook, what's with the birthday...
It's not my birthday.

1136
01:56:15,704 --> 01:56:20,573
Dieter, those two CIA dudes wanna take
you back to Guam for debriefing.

1137
01:56:21,343 --> 01:56:23,641
You don't wanna do that, do you?

1138
01:56:24,613 --> 01:56:26,240
I didn't think so.

1139
01:56:47,502 --> 01:56:48,935
Hey, hold on, guys.

1140
01:56:49,504 --> 01:56:53,406
Hey, guys, he's a bit choked up in there.

1141
01:56:54,176 --> 01:56:58,670
You mind giving him just a couple of
minutes to sort of pull himself together?

1142
01:56:58,780 --> 01:57:01,305
Yeah, it should be fine.
We'll give it a few minutes.

1143
01:57:01,416 --> 01:57:03,509
- He's a good kid, huh?
- Yeah.

1144
01:57:03,618 --> 01:57:05,279
- Thanks, guys.
- Yup.

1145
01:57:14,329 --> 01:57:20,029
MAN:... Right, left.
Left, left, left, right, left.

1146
01:57:24,973 --> 01:57:26,406
Come on, now.

1147
01:57:28,343 --> 01:57:30,470
Hurry up. Come on, get him in.

1148
01:57:31,646 --> 01:57:33,614
Get him in now, fast!

1149
01:57:33,715 --> 01:57:35,046
Get inside.

1150
01:57:48,330 --> 01:57:49,957
(WHOOPING) It's my day!

1151
01:58:00,542 --> 01:58:02,134
What are we doing?

1152
01:58:21,430 --> 01:58:22,658
DIETER: Hey.
SPOOK: What?

1153
01:58:22,764 --> 01:58:24,459
DIETER: Where is everybody?

1154
01:58:24,566 --> 01:58:25,555
- Where?
- Right here.

1155
01:58:25,667 --> 01:58:27,999
Why the decks... They're empty.
Have they gone home?

1156
01:58:28,103 --> 01:58:30,537
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

1157
01:58:31,106 --> 01:58:32,198
They're on vacation.

1158
01:58:32,307 --> 01:58:33,899
Is the war over?

1159
01:58:35,343 --> 01:58:36,435
No.

1160
01:58:42,384 --> 01:58:44,784
DIETER: You know I'm in a lot of trouble.

1161
01:58:51,726 --> 01:58:53,421
Boys, here he is.

1162
01:58:53,528 --> 01:58:55,894
They kidnapped him,
they brought him here to us.

1163
01:58:55,997 --> 01:58:59,057
The CIA held him for four days
but they can't hang onto him forever!

1164
01:58:59,167 --> 01:59:01,692
Dieter Dengler!

1165
01:59:07,843 --> 01:59:11,210
All right, all right. Hold on.
Hold on a second.

1166
01:59:11,313 --> 01:59:12,746
Boys, listen up for a second.

1167
01:59:12,848 --> 01:59:15,339
Admiral Willoughby's
got something to say.

1168
01:59:15,450 --> 01:59:17,145
Lieutenant Dengler.

1169
01:59:20,122 --> 01:59:21,953
Good to have you back.

1170
01:59:25,760 --> 01:59:27,694
- Thank you.
- All right. That's not all.

1171
01:59:27,796 --> 01:59:31,254
There's more! Hold on, fellows.
Hold on, hold on!

1172
01:59:32,334 --> 01:59:33,733
So, let's start with the man himself.

1173
01:59:33,835 --> 01:59:35,735
Dieter, it is just incredible
you made it home.

1174
01:59:35,837 --> 01:59:39,000
Now, tell us, was it your faith
in God and country?

1175
01:59:40,375 --> 01:59:42,969
Come on, Dieter,
you got to believe in something.

1176
01:59:43,078 --> 01:59:44,670
I believe I need a steak.

1177
01:59:44,779 --> 01:59:47,509
A steak! This guy needs a steak!

1178
01:59:47,616 --> 01:59:49,709
We're grilling up a big old cow for you.

1179
01:59:49,818 --> 01:59:52,912
All right. Hey, listen up. Hang on.

1180
01:59:53,021 --> 01:59:55,387
Can you pass something on to the boys?

1181
01:59:55,490 --> 01:59:57,048
You know, something you learned
during your ordeal,

1182
01:59:57,159 --> 02:00:01,118
something to keep them going
no matter how bad it gets?

1183
02:00:01,863 --> 02:00:03,228
Sure I can.

1184
02:00:05,934 --> 02:00:09,165
Empty what is full.

1185
02:00:10,539 --> 02:00:13,133
Fill what is empty.

1186
02:00:17,078 --> 02:00:19,911
Scratch where it itches. That's it.

1187
02:00:20,015 --> 02:00:21,676
Now look at these boys ' faces.

1188
02:00:21,783 --> 02:00:23,717
Do they love you, man!

1189
02:00:23,818 --> 02:00:27,447
Do they love you!
